1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,820
This doctor cracked the knuckles
on his left hand at least twice

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:04,490
a day, for more than fifty
years.

3
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:06,173
But he never once cracked his
right.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,160
Everyone warned him it would
give him arthritis.

5
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:09,920
So he decided to find out.

6
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:13,600
Inside every knuckle, the bones
sit in a capsule filled with a

7
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,790
slippery liquid called synovial
fluid.

8
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:17,895
When you pull the joint, the
bones separate,

9
00:00:17,905 --> 00:00:19,465
and the pressure inside drops.

10
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:22,155
Suddenly, a gas cavity forms in
the fluid.

11
00:00:22,495 --> 00:00:23,240
That's the pop.

12
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:26,740
In 2015, scientists filmed it
happening inside an

13
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:27,550
MRI scanner.

14
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:29,715
The gas takes about twenty
minutes to dissolve,

15
00:00:30,075 --> 00:00:32,495
which is why you can't crack the
same knuckle again right away.

16
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:35,153
After fifty years, he compared
his two hands.

17
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:38,132
Neither hand had arthritis, and
there was no difference between

18
00:00:38,142 --> 00:00:38,657
them.

19
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:41,247
In 2009, it won him an Ig Nobel
Prize.

20
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:42,508
So go ahead.

21
00:00:42,688 --> 00:00:43,488
Crack away.
